**Definition 1.4 (actual placement).** Keep CAP ports 0–63, their owners,
origins and routes. In particular verifier32–39, consumer40–47 and routes50–51
remain occupied. Reuse exactly ARC's $A$-owned annex:

| Ports | Use |
| --- | --- |
| 64,65 | Immutable alternating word banks, with actual parity. |
| 66,67 | Native base/ordinal and length scratch, respectively. |
| 68 | RCA-format, zero-based descriptors, with F and seal. |
| 69 | Actual code capture, initial manifest fields and later staging. |
| 70 | Retained gate, HistoryMode and history-frame ingress. |
| 71 | Immutable cover/package/image backing and sender blocks. |
| 72,73 | Dedicated mailbox and actual receiver. |

The handler, client and mailbox availability slots are distinct even though
their principal is $A$. The new compiler never borrows the producer's twelve
workspace tokens. Closed reads of 26/28/29 use ARC §3's actual read rights
and restore those heads. CAP29's ten sep-delimited fields and one-based
creation ordinals are parsed separately from annex68's RCA unary/flags/F
grammar. Port number, native base, complete reference, event ordinal,
cycle index, cover/package number and primitive tally have separate types.

